%description:
Tests minshallNagle=true, the Nagle of Minshall that Linux uses
(tcp_minshall_check()). The client writes 2600 bytes in two writes and 100
bytes at t=1.3. After the ACK of t=1.203, the tail of 600 bytes goes at once
after the full segment, although that segment is not acknowledged: only a small
segment holds. With the Nagle of RFC 9293 section 3.7.4 (the default), the tail
would wait for the ACK of t=1.407. The write of t=1.3 waits, because the tail
of 600 bytes is a small segment that is not acknowledged yet.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 2500; 1.001 100; 1.3 100"
*.*_tcp.mss = 1000
*.cli_tcp.minshallNagle = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:1001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 1001 win 16384 
[1.205 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1001:2001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.205 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A 2001:2601(600) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.407 B003] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 2601 win 16384 
[1.409 A006] A.1000 > B.2000: A 2601:2701(100) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.611 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 2701 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
